  <id value="WHOHivToNgHivLocal"/>
  <text>
    <status value="generated"/><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p class="res-header-id"><b>Generated Narrative: ConceptMap WHOHivToNgHivLocal</b></p><a name="WHOHivToNgHivLocal"> </a><a name="hcWHOHivToNgHivLocal"> </a><p>Mapping from http://smart.who.int/hiv/CodeSystem/HIVConcepts to (not specified)</p><br/><p><b>Group 1 </b>Mapping from <code>http://smart.who.int/hiv/CodeSystem/HIVConcepts|1.0.0</code> to <a href="CodeSystem-ng-hiv-art-follow-up-status-cs.html">HIV Follow Up Status CodeSystem</a></p><table class="grid"><tr><td><b>Source Code</b></td><td><b>Relationship</b></td><td><b>Target Code</b></td><td><b>Comment</b></td></tr><tr><td>HIV.H.DE42 (Lost to follow-up)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#equivalent" title="equivalent">is equivalent to</a></td><td>lost (Lost to follow-up)</td><td>WHO and Nigeria concepts represent loss to follow-up in HIV treatment follow-up.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.H.DE43 (Transferred out)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#equivalent" title="equivalent">is equivalent to</a></td><td>to (Transferred out)</td><td>Nigeria 'to' is the established local code for transferred out.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.H.DE44 (Death (documented))</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>dead</td><td>WHO explicitly requires documented death; the Nigeria local concept is broader.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.D.DE45 (Restarting ART)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#equivalent" title="equivalent">is equivalent to</a></td><td>restart (Restart ART)</td><td>Both represent restarting ART after an interruption.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.D.DE40 (Stopped ART)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#equivalent" title="equivalent">is equivalent to</a></td><td>stop (Stopped ART)</td><td>Both represent ART having been stopped.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.H.DE45 (Refused (stopped) treatment)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>stop (Stopped ART)</td><td>WHO is narrower because it specifies confirmed refusal/stopping treatment.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.H.DE47 (On ART)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#equivalent" title="equivalent">is equivalent to</a></td><td>alive-on-art</td><td>Both indicate that the client is currently alive and receiving ART.</td></tr></table><hr/><p><b>Group 2 </b>Mapping from <code>http://smart.who.int/hiv/CodeSystem/HIVConcepts|1.0.0</code> to <a href="CodeSystem-ng-hiv-arv-adherence-cs.html">HIV-ARV Adherence CodeSystem</a></p><table class="grid"><tr><td><b>Source Code</b></td><td><b>Relationship</b></td><td><b>Target Code</b></td><td><b>Comment</b></td></tr><tr><td>HIV.D.DE40 (Stopped ART)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>Stopped</td><td>The Nigeria code is used in an adherence/status context while WHO states treatment status.</td></tr></table><hr/><p><b>Group 3 </b>Mapping from <code>http://smart.who.int/hiv/CodeSystem/HIVConcepts|1.0.0</code> to <a href="CodeSystem-ng-hiv-dsd-reason-for-category-change-cs.html">HIV DSD - Reason For Category Change CodeSystem</a></p><table class="grid"><tr><td><b>Source Code</b></td><td><b>Relationship</b></td><td><b>Target Code</b></td><td><b>Comment</b></td></tr><tr><td>HIV.H.DE42 (Lost to follow-up)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#equivalent" title="equivalent">is equivalent to</a></td><td>Lost</td><td/></tr><tr><td>HIV.H.DE43 (Transferred out)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#equivalent" title="equivalent">is equivalent to</a></td><td>TO (Transferred out)</td><td/></tr><tr><td>HIV.H.DE44 (Death (documented))</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>Dead</td><td>WHO is narrower because it specifies documented death.</td></tr></table><hr/><p><b>Group 4 </b>Mapping from <code>http://smart.who.int/hiv/CodeSystem/HIVConcepts|1.0.0</code> to <a href="CodeSystem-ng-hiv-positive-tracking-cs.html">HIV Positive Tracking</a></p><table class="grid"><tr><td><b>Source Code</b></td><td><b>Relationship</b></td><td><b>Target Code</b></td><td><b>Comment</b></td></tr><tr><td>HIV.H.DE4 (Did not initiate ART)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#equivalent" title="equivalent">is equivalent to</a></td><td>Not-Started (ART not started)</td><td/></tr><tr><td>HIV.D.DE382 (ART initiated within 7 days of diagnosis)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>Started-ART</td><td>Nigeria is broader because it does not restrict ART initiation to seven days.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.B.DE147 (Linked to enrolment in care and ART initiation)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>Linked-To-Care</td><td>WHO includes enrolment linkage and ART initiation; the Nigeria concept represents linkage to care.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.H.DE41 (HIV treatment outcome)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>Final-Outcome</td><td>Nigeria represents the final tracking outcome; WHO represents the treatment outcome used for retention/attrition.</td></tr></table><hr/><p><b>Group 5 </b>Mapping from <code>http://smart.who.int/hiv/CodeSystem/HIVConcepts|1.0.0</code> to <a href="CodeSystem-ng-hiv-final-outcome-cs.html">HIV - Final Outcome CodeSystem</a></p><table class="grid"><tr><td><b>Source Code</b></td><td><b>Relationship</b></td><td><b>Target Code</b></td><td><b>Comment</b></td></tr><tr><td>HIV.H.DE42 (Lost to follow-up)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#equivalent" title="equivalent">is equivalent to</a></td><td>lost-to-follow-up</td><td/></tr><tr><td>HIV.H.DE44 (Death (documented))</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>died</td><td>WHO explicitly requires documented death; the Nigeria outcome is broader.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.H.DE45 (Refused (stopped) treatment)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>declined</td><td>Nigeria 'declined' is broader than WHO's confirmed refusal/stopping treatment.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.D.DE382 (ART initiated within 7 days of diagnosis)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>started-art</td><td>Nigeria is broader because it does not specify the seven-day initiation window.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.H.DE49 (Transfer confirmed)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>confirmed-referral</td><td>Both describe confirmed onward movement, but WHO is specifically a confirmed transfer.</td></tr></table><hr/><p><b>Group 6 </b>Mapping from <code>http://smart.who.int/hiv/CodeSystem/HIVConcepts|1.0.0</code> to <a href="CodeSystem-ng-hiv-reason-not-started-art-cs.html">HIV - Reason Not Started ART CodeSystem</a></p><table class="grid"><tr><td><b>Source Code</b></td><td><b>Relationship</b></td><td><b>Target Code</b></td><td><b>Comment</b></td></tr><tr><td>HIV.D.DE371 (Patient self-reported as not ready/willing)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>declined</td><td>Not ready/willing is narrower than the local declined category.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.D.DE372 (Not completed education, support and preparation for ART)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>on-adherence-preparation</td><td>Both describe preparation/support before ART initiation, but the local category is broader.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.H.DE47 (On ART)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>known-positive-on-art</td><td>Local code is used as a reason not to newly initiate a person already known to be on ART.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.D.DE377 (Patient diagnosed with cryptococcal meningitis)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>on-oi-management</td><td>Cryptococcal meningitis is a specific opportunistic infection within the broader local OI-management category.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.D.DE378 (Patient diagnosed with histoplasmosis)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>on-oi-management</td><td>Histoplasmosis is a specific opportunistic infection within the broader local OI-management category.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.D.DE380 (Other)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#equivalent" title="equivalent">is equivalent to</a></td><td>other</td><td>Both are the residual other-reason category for delayed/non-initiation of ART.</td></tr></table><hr/><p><b>Group 7 </b>Mapping from <code>http://smart.who.int/hiv/CodeSystem/HIVConcepts|1.0.0</code> to <a href="CodeSystem-ng-hiv-target-population-category-cs.html">Target Population Category Codes</a></p><table class="grid"><tr><td><b>Source Code</b></td><td><b>Relationship</b></td><td><b>Target Code</b></td><td><b>Comment</b></td></tr><tr><td>HIV.B.DE51 (Sex worker)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>Female-Commercial-Sex-Workers</td><td>WHO includes sex workers generally; the Nigeria target category is female-specific.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.B.DE52 (Men who have sex with men)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#equivalent" title="equivalent">is equivalent to</a></td><td>MSM (Men who have sex with men)</td><td/></tr><tr><td>HIV.B.DE53 (Trans and gender-diverse people)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>TG (Transgender)</td><td>WHO explicitly includes gender-diverse people in addition to transgender people.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.B.DE54 (People who inject drugs)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#equivalent" title="equivalent">is equivalent to</a></td><td>People-Who-Inject-Drug (People who inject drugs)</td><td/></tr><tr><td>HIV.B.DE58 (Orphan or vulnerable child)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>OVC-AIDS-Orphaned (OVC/AIDS orphaned)</td><td>WHO is broader than the Nigeria category, which is specifically HIV/AIDS-oriented.</td></tr></table><hr/><p><b>Group 8 </b>Mapping from <code>http://smart.who.int/hiv/CodeSystem/HIVConcepts|1.0.0</code> to <a href="CodeSystem-ng-tb-tpt-prophylaxis-type-cs.html">TB TPT Prophylaxis Type Codes</a></p><table class="grid"><tr><td><b>Source Code</b></td><td><b>Relationship</b></td><td><b>Target Code</b></td><td><b>Comment</b></td></tr><tr><td>HIV.D.DE250 (Provide isoniazid preventive therapy)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>inh (Isoniazid preventive therapy)</td><td>WHO represents the service/action; Nigeria represents the local prophylaxis type.</td></tr></table><hr/><p><b>Group 9 </b>Mapping from <code>http://smart.who.int/hiv/CodeSystem/HIVConcepts|1.0.0</code> to <a href="CodeSystem-ng-hiv-enhanced-adherence-counselling-status-cs.html">Enhanced Adherence Counselling</a></p><table class="grid"><tr><td><b>Source Code</b></td><td><b>Relationship</b></td><td><b>Target Code</b></td><td><b>Comment</b></td></tr><tr><td>HIV.D.DE496 (Enhanced adherence counselling provided)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>eac (Enhanced adherence counselling)</td><td>WHO represents provision of EAC; Nigeria represents the EAC concept itself.</td></tr></table><hr/><p><b>Group 10 </b>Mapping from <code>http://smart.who.int/hiv/CodeSystem/HIVConcepts|1.0.0</code> to <a href="CodeSystem-ng-hiv-care-art-codes-cs.html">NG HIV Care and ART Codes</a></p><table class="grid"><tr><td><b>Source Code</b></td><td><b>Relationship</b></td><td><b>Target Code</b></td><td><b>Comment</b></td></tr><tr><td>HIV.D.DE223 (Other reason for stopping ART)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#equivalent" title="equivalent">is equivalent to</a></td><td>art-stop-reason-10 (Other reason for stopping ART)</td><td/></tr><tr><td>HIV.D.DE425 (Other reason for regimen substitution)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>regimen-change-reason-10 (Other regimen change reason)</td><td>Nigeria combines substitution/switch reasons; WHO is specifically substitution.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.D.DE434 (Other)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>regimen-change-reason-10 (Other regimen change reason)</td><td>WHO code is specifically other within regimen switch; Nigeria combines substitution/switch reasons.</td></tr></table><hr/><p><b>Group 11 </b>Mapping from <code>http://smart.who.int/hiv/CodeSystem/HIVConcepts|1.0.0</code> to <a href="CodeSystem-ng-hiv-eac-form-cs.html">NG HIV Enhanced Adherence Counselling Form Codes</a></p><table class="grid"><tr><td><b>Source Code</b></td><td><b>Relationship</b></td><td><b>Target Code</b></td></tr><tr><td>HIV.D.DE215 (Other reason for nonadherence)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#equivalent" title="equivalent">is equivalent to</a></td><td>barrier-other (Other adherence barrier)</td></tr></table><hr/><p><b>Group 12 </b>Mapping from <code>http://smart.who.int/hiv/CodeSystem/HIVConcepts|1.0.0</code> to <a href="CodeSystem-ng-hiv-int-lab-form-cs.html">NG HIV Integrated Laboratory Form Codes</a></p><table class="grid"><tr><td><b>Source Code</b></td><td><b>Relationship</b></td><td><b>Target Code</b></td><td><b>Comment</b></td></tr><tr><td>HIV.B.DE84 (Nucleic acid test for HIV)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>test-type-eid (Early infant diagnosis)</td><td>WHO describes the virological test method; Nigeria uses an EID programme test-type category.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.D.DE406 (HIV viral load test ordered)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>test-type-viral-load (Viral load)</td><td>WHO represents the order action; Nigeria represents the requested test type.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.D.DE364 (CD4 count)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>other-test-cd4-count (CD4 count)</td><td>WHO represents the CD4 count data element; Nigeria code identifies the requested/recorded test type.</td></tr><tr><td>HIV.D.DE365 (CD4 cell percentage)</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-concept-map-relationship.html#inexact" title="inexact">maps loosely to</a></td><td>other-test-cd4-percentage (CD4 percentage)</td><td>WHO represents the CD4 percentage data element; Nigeria code identifies the requested/recorded test type.</td></tr></table></div>
